# Describe the skills this robot offers to missions.
---
# JSON: catalog_version, learnable (the leaves a taught skill may be built from), and skills, each
# with its name, description, args (type, names, format, enum, min and max, default_from,
# narrowed), the outputs it hands on, requires, effects, resources, idempotent, risk,
# max_duration_s, learned and taught_for for a taught one, and the template: the ID of the skill's
# macro SubTree.
string catalog_json
# BehaviorTree.CPP's TreeNodesModel XML: the leaves' models, then a SubTree entry for each skill's
# macro. A mission may use only those SubTrees and the plain control nodes, never a leaf.
string tree_nodes_model_xml
string bt_cpp_version
# Changes whenever the catalog or the node model changes. It is the version of whoever answers:
# a composite in front of the executor answers its own, which the executor's DefineSkill and
# ForgetSkill replies do not carry.
string catalog_version
